# diagnostic-mode: compile
# expect-code: E2S158
# expect-span: byte 887
# The block-bodied trailing lambda of `spec/syntax/call-arguments-v1.md`
# (#880). The expression body is lowered by #1191; the block body is accepted
# design and not current capability, because Stage 2 parses no block-body
# lambda in any spelling.
#
# The span is the `fn` that opens the lambda, not the call it attaches to,
# because that is the token the author would rewrite to make the program
# compile today.
#
# Refusing by name matters more here than for a shape nobody can write: a
# block body makes `lambda_parameters_end` span to -1, so without this the
# trailing lambda is re-read as the start of the next declaration and the
# author is blamed for a token they did not get wrong.
fn apply(value: Int, action: Int -> Int) -> Int {
    return action(value)
}

fn main() -> Int {
    print(apply(1) fn(x) {
        return x
    })
    return 0
}
